Process/CLI final regression:
  go test -race ./cmd/syncer -count=3 -timeout=90s
  PASS 8.547s.
  Each process lifecycle case starts two real test-binary child processes through
  mainWithSignals, reaches PSYNC, sends SIGTERM, and observes normal exit plus
  source connection EOF. The second process reopens the same empty manifest and
  LOCK inode and reaches PSYNC again. Three runs cover six starts/stops.
  Backends are controlled RESP fixtures. They return no RDB and accept no business
  writes; this verifies process signaling/lock lifecycle, NOT database correctness
  or data resume. All children and fixture connections are joined in cleanup.

